Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-23-2001||12:06 AM||||Is the 9.7 compression number correct when used with Fieros cast heads? Are they a direct replacement for the stock pistons, with no modifications having to be made to them to work? This would still run OK on 92 octane gas, right? I can get a set of these for considerably less than a set of forged 9.5 ration pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierosound||03-23-2001||12:15 AM||||Read through this thread  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008285.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008285.html</A> <P>I have the DOHC pistons in my 3.4L.  I run premium with nor problems.  In a recent compression test, I'm hitting around 225 PSI compression in all cylinders.||||reg||10
